These are particularly mutagenic. Now, that's some of the classic tumors that are associated with cigarette smoke.

81
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:12,920
But I want to remind you that also associated with smoking and cigarette smoke is kidney and bladder cancer.

82
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:21,920
Now, generally speaking, the urothelium, which is the lining of the collecting system of the kidney, the bladder, the ureters,

83
00:09:21,920 --> 00:09:28,920
and a portion of the urethra, that entire system is lined by urothelium.

84
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:34,920
And the key risk factor for urothelial carcinoma, cigarette smoke, cigarette smoke, cigarette smoke.

85
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:40,920
And the idea here is that when a patient smokes, the carcinogens get into the blood, and then they get filtered by the kidney,

86
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:44,920
and they get concentrated in the urine. And when they get concentrated in the urine,

87
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:51,920
they sort of hang out in the bladder, and in the ureter, and in the collecting system, as fluid is sort of washing those areas.

88
00:09:51,920 --> 00:10:00,920
And basically, the entire collecting system, the entire urothelium, is being bathed with carcinogen constantly over a period of years.

89
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:07,920
And so cigarette smoke is the key risk factor for both kidney and bladder cancer.

90
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:11,920
Alright, so that's the association with cigarette smoke.

